# E04 Shapley Value: parallel. RandomAgent of the C# takes the agent in the order of a ConcurrentDictionary, whose
# string hash changes from one run to the next in .NET Core: two runs of the C# already pick other workers (the C++
# picks in insertion order, from the same draws). The manager also matches the time estimates with the workers in their
# order of arrival. Compared: the counts of every kind of line, every worker reporting once, and the total of the
# rewards, the total of the prices of the tasks drawn from the seed of the oracle (3 648), within the rounding of 27 F3
# values.
cover all
fact selected ^Selected: (worker\d{3}) (worker\d{3}) (worker\d{3})$
fact time ^\t\[(worker\d{3}) -> manager\]: time (\d+) (\d+) (\d+)$
fact results ^\t\[shapley -> manager\]: results (.*)$
fact calculate ^\t\[manager -> shapley\]: calculate (.*)$
fact finished ^Manager has finished$
fact report ^Agent (worker\d{3}) has (-?\d+\.\d{3})$
same selected count
same time count
same results count
same calculate count
same finished count
same report count
check report count == 27
check report distinct(0) == 27
check report sum(1) in [3647.98,3648.02]
